The Pea-Peach project has been updated, release 0.12 is now available
for download (sources, cdocumentation, binaries for Linux and Windows)
at
https://sourceforge.net/projects/pea-peach
Update is recommended.

Changelog:
- bugfix of CRC64 related code;
- new feature: the job definition can be saved as plaintext (it can be
useful as starting point for understanding how to compose pea-peach
related scripts);
- some minor interface improvements:
-- more information displayed in Peach stringgrid (object's last
modification time and attributes);
-- HowTo panel added for exemplifying program's functions (how to
archive files, how to use encryption, how to split files, change
program's behaviour and aspect etc);
- Linux binaries released as .tar.gz;
- project rebuild with latest Lazarus release (0.9.18).

