I have developed a small (only 103MB) Linux Distribution called ZeroShell 
for network server applications. It is now available in the form of live cd 
or of compact flash image for embedded devices with which it is possible to 
build network appliances. Yesterday, I released the version 1.0.beta2 in 
which the main new feature is the presence of a captive portal to 
authenticate the user of a wireless network by using web login. This type of 
authentication is often used in the Hotel, Hotspot or other places where it 
is necessary to authorize the network accesses.
ZeroShell can provides many others services that are described on the home 
page http://www.zeroshell.net/eng such as: Radius server, DNS and DHCP 
server, routing and bridging, vlan, VPN lan-to-lan and host-to-lan, virtual 
servers, ldap authorization and kerberos authentication, x.509 certification 
authority, network time server, dynamic dns, xDSL and cable connection 
client, Firewall.
I

